Hi [PERSON_3],

Thanks for the list of open points. These ones all sit with us, so here is where
each one stands. None of them are decided or delivered yet, but they are ours to
sort out, not something you need to guess at.

- Carrier label formats: we ship with three carriers. Each carrier has to send us
  its current label and manifest specification, and we will forward them to you.
  We have asked, but nothing has come back yet, and one carrier is moving to a
  new label format next year.
- Label printers: we haven't decided whether to keep the existing Zebra printers
  on the packing benches or buy new ones as part of this project. Facilities will
  make that call once the budget is approved.
- Building drawings and floor survey: the landlord holds the as-built drawings
  and the floor flatness survey for the new building. We will request them and
  pass them on, but we don't have a date from the landlord yet.
- Network: our IT team will provide the network for the automation (VLANs, IP
  ranges, firewall rules and the wireless coverage in the chilled zone). We
  haven't designed it yet and we will need your requirements first.
- Remote access: any vendor access to the site systems has to go through our own
  remote access gateway. Security has to approve your engineers' accounts one by
  one, and that approval normally takes about three weeks.
- Chilled zone layout: the operations team still has to sign off the final
  chilled zone layout, including where the dock doors and the air curtains go.
  Sign-off is planned for November.
- Test orders: our business team will prepare a representative set of test
  orders and the expected results for acceptance testing, but they won't start
  on that until the design is agreed.

Please price on the basis that we deliver these. If any of them is critical for
your plan, tell us by when you need it and we will put it in our project plan.

